jobs.description:
Company Introduction
AMBIKA STEEL SOLUTIONS' original business focused on the manufacturing, supply, and international trade of industrial steel, pipes, flanges, fasteners, and related products.

To drive business diversification and digitalization, the company is preparing to launch a fintech and blockchain business in Phoenix, Arizona, with plans to establish an independently operating U.S. subsidiary. This subsidiary will focus on exploring solutions for enterprise payments, supply chain finance, blockchain infrastructure, digital fund management, and compliant financial technology.

The new business is currently in the preparation and transformation phase. Specific products and services will be determined based on company approvals and market conditions.
Job Overview
The Chief Operating Officer will be responsible for the establishment and daily operation of the new Phoenix business, assisting in developing a business plan, establishing the organizational structure, recruiting the core team, and coordinating technology, finance, risk, legal, and compliance functions.

Key Responsibilities

Responsible for the establishment and operational planning of new businesses in the United States;

Develop organizational structure, annual budget, and key performance indicators;

Establish operational, financial, risk, and internal control systems;

Recruit and manage technology, product, compliance, and operations teams;

Drive enterprise payment and blockchain infrastructure projects;

Evaluate supply chain finance and digital treasury management solutions;

Coordinate with lawyers, accountants, banks, and regulatory advisors;

Ensure necessary permits and approvals are obtained before business commencement;

Manage relationships with suppliers, technology partners, and financial institutions;

Report regularly to the CEO and Board of Directors on the progress of establishment and operations.

Job Requirements

Bachelor's degree or above, preferably in finance, business administration, law, or technology;

15+ years of operational management experience, including 10+ years of senior management experience;

Experience in fintech, payments, banking, or blockchain industries;

Familiar with U.S. company operations, budgeting, and risk management;

Understand AML, KYC, data security, and financial regulatory requirements;

Experience building a team or new business from scratch;

Excellent leadership, communication, and cross-departmental collaboration skills;
Must be legally qualified to work in the United States.

Salary and Compensation

Suggested base annual salary: $175,000–$250,000 USD
Annual performance bonus and long-term incentives are also available. Final salary will be determined based on experience, responsibilities, and company budget.

Benefits

Medical, dental, and vision insurance;

401(k) retirement plan;

Paid annual leave and sick leave;

Annual performance bonus;

Professional training and certification support;

Co-working space;

Relocation support, subject to availability;

Equity or long-term incentive plans, subject to company policy.

